menu "CrowPanel 1.46in board"

comment "Display"

config CROWPANEL_LCD_BGR
    bool "Panel expects BGR element order"
    default n
    help
      Swaps red and blue. n (RGB) is VERIFIED on hardware (TrailCurrent
      Capstan), against a deliberate red/green/blue test pattern rather than
      a screen of UI chrome, which will not show a red/blue swap.

      This is the OPPOSITE of the 1.28in board, which needs y. They are
      different controllers driving differently-bonded glass; do not copy
      one board's value to the other.

      Do not derive this from the vendor's LovyanGFX `cfg.rgb_order`
      either (true on this board). It does not map onto esp_lcd's element
      order the way the name suggests -- on both CrowPanels it is the exact
      inverse of what the panel needs.

config CROWPANEL_LCD_MIRROR_X
    bool "Mirror the display horizontally"
    default n
    help
      n is what the TrailCurrent Capstan firmware runs on this board. The
      1.28in needs y; this panel does not. If text reads backwards --
      mirrored rather than upside down -- flip this.

      This flips the DISPLAY only. The touch layer has its own options
      below, and the two are independent.

config CROWPANEL_LCD_MIRROR_Y
    bool "Mirror the display vertically"
    default n
    help
      With MIRROR_X this gives a 180-degree rotation, for a panel mounted
      upside down. Mirror the touch to match.

comment "Touch"

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_MIRROR_X
    bool "Mirror touch horizontally"
    default n
    help
      Independent of the display transform. The touch controller is a
      separate device whose axes are fixed by how ITS layer is bonded, so
      work this out on the glass rather than copying the display setting.

      NOT YET VERIFIED on this board: Capstan, where the rest of this board
      layer comes from, keeps touch off. If a tap on the left lands on the
      right, set this.

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_MIRROR_Y
    bool "Mirror touch vertically"
    default n
    help
      NOT YET VERIFIED on this board -- see CROWPANEL_TOUCH_MIRROR_X.

config CROWPANEL_TOUCH_SWAP_XY
    bool "Swap touch X and Y axes"
    default n

comment "Rotary ring"

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_STEPS_PER_DETENT
    int "Quadrature counts per detent"
    range 1 8
    default 2
    help
      Counts the 4x quadrature decoder produces per mechanical detent.
      VERIFIED on hardware: 2. At 4 it takes two detents to move once.

      The 1.28in is 4 -- the two boards are pin-identical but do NOT share
      an encoder, and neither value may be derived from the other. Enable
      CROWPANEL_ENCODER_DEBUG and turn one detent to measure a different
      unit.

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_INVERT
    bool "Invert rotation direction"
    default n
    help
      Clockwise must increase. NOT YET VERIFIED on this board: n matches
      the 1.28in, and Capstan records the 1.46in as unconfirmed. If
      clockwise moves the selection backwards on your unit, set this.

config CROWPANEL_ENCODER_DEBUG
    bool "Log raw encoder counts"
    default n

config CROWPANEL_LONG_PRESS_MS
    int "Ring long-press duration (ms)"
    range 300 3000
    default 700

comment "LED ring"

config CROWPANEL_LEDS_MAX_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Maximum LED ring brightness (percent)"
    range 1 100
    default 100
    help
      Ceiling applied to every LED write. 100 is full scale, the brightest
      the WS2812s go. Lower it if the ring is too bright in a dark room
      (TrailCurrent Capstan runs this board at 40 on a wall).

endmenu
